        <!-- Hero Video -->
        {% if zh %}<section class="media-block full-width" style="position:relative; background:#0d0d0d; border: 1px solid rgba(255,255,255,0.05); overflow:hidden;">{% else %}<section class="media-block full-width media-block--video">{% endif %}
          <div class="arc-video-label">Demo Footage</div>
          <video autoplay="" muted="" loop="" playsinline="" class="block-video--hero">
            <source src="/images/Project/ARCCSRL-Robotic-Limb/Footage.mp4" type="video/mp4">
          </video>
        </section>

        <!-- Human 2.0 at MIT -->
        <section class="content-grid-2col">
          <div class="text-section">
            <span class="section-kicker">{% if zh %}總覽{% else %}Overview{% endif %}</span>
            <h3>Human 2.0 At MIT</h3>
            <p>{% if zh %}這門 MIT Media Lab 課程深入探索當前與未來應用於人體認知、情感、社交及身體增強的核心技術原理。主題涵蓋機器人外骨骼與矯形器、肢體義肢、神經植入物、社交情感義肢，以及認知義肢等前沿研究領域。{% else %}
              This MIT Media Lab course delves into the principles underlying current and future technologies for
              cognitive, emotional, social, and physical augmentation. Topics span robotic exoskeletons and orthoses,
              limb prostheses, neural implants, social-emotional prostheses, and cognitive prostheses at the cutting
              edge of human augmentation research.
            {% endif %}</p>
            <p>{% if zh %}Harry 在課程中以多媒體設計師的身份參與研究團隊，透過設計專業將複雜的科學資訊轉化為清晰、具說服力的視覺語言，從實驗圖表到最終簡報，全程貫穿整個研究週期。{% else %}
              Harry joined the research team as a multimedia designer, translating complex scientific information into
              clear and compelling visual language — from experimental diagrams to the final presentation — throughout
              the entire research cycle.
            {% endif %}</p>
            <ul class="arc-role-list">
              <li>{% if zh %}仿生機電學 — Hugh Herr 教授主講，涵蓋動力義肢與外骨骼{% else %}Biomechatronics — Powered Prostheses &amp;
                Exoskeletons by Prof. Hugh Herr{% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}神經介面 — 周邊神經介面、腦機介面與神經感知義肢{% else %}Neural Interfaces — Peripheral &amp; Central Neuroprostheses
              {% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}人體實驗設計 — MIT COUHES 人類受試者測試規範與實驗方法{% else %}Human Subject Testing — MIT COUHES Experimental
                Design{% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}學期專案 — 自選人類增強主題，完成實驗並發表論文品質報告{% else %}Semester Project — Human Augmentation Research &amp;
                Publication{% endif %}</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
          <div class="media-block media-block--flush">
            <div class="image-wrapper">
              <img src="/images/Project/ARCCSRL-Robotic-Limb/MIT%20(2).webp" alt="MIT Media Lab Research Team" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </div>
        </section>

        <!-- AR x Robotic Limb Section -->
        <section class="content-grid-2col">
          <div class="media-block media-block--flush">
            <div class="image-wrapper">
              <img src="/images/Project/ARCCSRL-Robotic-Limb/HoloLens%20Device%20Mockup.webp" alt="HoloLens AR Mockup" loading="lazy">
            </div>
          </div>
          <div class="text-section">
            <span class="section-kicker">{% if zh %}技術核心{% else %}Technology{% endif %}</span>
            <h3>{% if zh %}AR X 機械義肢{% else %}AR X ROBOTIC LIMB{% endif %}</h3>
            <p>{% if zh %}Harry 協助 ARCCSRL 團隊為 MIT Media Lab 研發的連續型機械義肢搭建 HoloLens 視覺輔助 GUI。這套 AR 介面整合了眼球追蹤技術與語音指令，讓使用者得以在完全不接觸義肢的情況下，透過直覺的凝視與聲音直接操控肢體動作。{% else %}
              Harry assisted the ARCCSRL team in building the HoloLens visual-assist GUI for the continuous robotic
              limb developed at MIT Media Lab. This AR interface integrates eye-gaze tracking and voice commands,
              enabling users to intuitively control limb movements without any physical contact.
            {% endif %}</p>
            <p>{% if zh %}為了確保介面在混合現實環境下的可讀性，Harry 協助設計 HoloLens 上的浮動 UI 元件，包含狀態指示器、操作提示與即時回饋視覺，讓使用者在配戴設備時能即時掌握義肢的控制狀態。{% else %}
              To ensure readability in mixed reality environments, Harry assisted in designing floating UI components
              for HoloLens — including status indicators, operation prompts, and real-time feedback visuals — enabling
              users to instantly understand prosthetic control states while wearing the device.
            {% endif %}</p>
            <ul class="arc-role-list">
              <li>{% if zh %}HoloLens GUI 介面協助搭建{% else %}HoloLens GUI Development{% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}混合現實 UI 元件設計{% else %}Mixed Reality UI Components{% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}使用者測試數據視覺化{% else %}User Testing Data Visualization{% endif %}</li>
              <li>{% if zh %}協助使用者實驗{% else %}Supporting User Experiments{% endif %}</li>
            </ul>
          </div>
        </section>

